Local customizations (diff from upstream)
-----------------------------------------
- deslop: description tightened to be branch-diff-scoped and AI-slop-specific,
  with an explicit disambiguation note vs the `code-simplifier` skill.
- verify-this: added a one-line positioning note distinguishing it from the
  Thoven `verify` skill (pre-commit task-completion checks).
- thermo-nuclear agent: renamed the plugin reference from "cursor-team-kit" to
  "team-kit"; adapted the parent-orchestration note from Cursor's subagent_type
  "shell"/"explore" to Claude Code's Bash + Read/Explore + Agent; and scoped the
  description to STRUCTURAL maintainability only, with an explicit boundary vs the
  `code-reviewer` agent (correctness/security/requirements) so auto-routing on
  description match does not collide.

NOT ported (intentionally — see the plan / repo docs)
-----------------------------------------------------
ci-watcher, run-smoke-tests, what-did-i-get-done, and all PR-flow skills
(make-pr-easy-to-review, new-branch-and-pr, get-pr-comments, pr-review-canvas,
review-and-ship), plus loop-on-ci, fix-ci, control-cli, control-ui,
check-compiler-errors, fix-merge-conflicts, workflow-from-chats, and the two
.mdc rules. Reasons: solo-dev/Replit workflow, missing Playwright smoke suite,
or already covered by existing Thoven skills.

Re-vendoring (staying current with upstream)
--------------------------------------------
There is no auto-update. To pull newer upstream versions, re-run the fetch at a
newer commit, re-apply the customizations above, bump the plugin version, and
review the diff before committing:

  REPO=cursor/plugins; SHA=<new-commit-sha>
  gh api "repos/$REPO/contents/cursor-team-kit/skills/<name>/SKILL.md?ref=$SHA" \
    -H "Accept: application/vnd.github.raw" > skills/<name>/SKILL.md

Addition: thermo-nuclear-review + thermos (2026-07-23)
-------------------------------------------------------
Upstream restructured: Cursor split `thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review` out of
`cursor-team-kit` into a new standalone plugin, `thermos`, alongside a new deep
correctness/security-review skill (`thermo-nuclear-review`) and an orchestrator
skill (`thermos`) that runs both in parallel and synthesizes findings. Upstream's
own migration note: "Remove the old thermo entries from team-kit when you install
this plugin to avoid duplicates" — not applicable here since we vendor content
directly rather than installing the Cursor plugin.

